# Hopper's NetBird patches, in apply order (later ones build on earlier ones).
# Second word on: phone = the app's library (app/scripts/build-engine.sh), exit = the exit servers' client
# (exit-server/scripts/build.sh, copied to the public repo by publish.sh).
# A line with "wireguard" applies to the wireguard-go checkout instead of NetBird.

# gRPC to Management and Signal: with NB_GRPC_WEBSOCKET=true it rides the self-hosted server's WebSocket wrapper, for hosts behind a proxy that does not pass gRPC; and the reconnect wait is capped at 30 s, down from 120 s, so a client reaches a server soon after it wakes.
netbird-grpc-dialer.patch phone exit
# Each peer update switches on Maybenot padding when NB_DAITA_MACHINES holds machines, and full-size packets when NB_DAITA_FULL_SIZE=true.
netbird-daita.patch phone exit
# Connections to the host in NB_ECH_HOST use ECH after a DNS-over-HTTPS lookup, or are refused; QUIC to it is skipped.
netbird-ech.patch phone exit
# The answer goes out before ICE candidates, and each new ICE agent gets the remote candidates of the last 5 s, so a direct link can form in the first round instead of after minutes on the relay. Drop this once netbirdio/netbird#8443 is fixed upstream.
netbird-ice-first-round.patch phone exit
# Mullvad's DAITA ported to the batched send path, with the Maybenot BlockOutgoing action; built with Rust maybenot-ffi for arm64.
wireguard-daita.patch wireguard phone exit
